id: pm-t310hx
title: Exact-tag npm recovery must stabilize public package access before verification
description: "A workflow_dispatch rerun for an immutable published tag can observe stale anonymous public metadata, skip npm access recovery, pass isolated verification, and leave the package private seconds later. Harden exact-tag recovery so public access is explicitly restored before anonymous package/version probes and remains verified without republishing or moving the tag."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T00:05:13.668Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T20:42:20.668Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-31T01:03:14.623Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-31T01:03:14.623Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "workflow_dispatch recovery explicitly sets @unbrained/pm-cli public before anonymous probes; existing immutable versions are never republished or retagged; executable workflow contracts cover recovery ordering and failure behavior; the existing v2026.7.30 tag is recovered and independently verifies through npm, npx, and bunx"
parent: pm-7zs0
risk: high
severity: high
resolution: fixed
expected_result: "Exact-tag recovery restores public access from a reviewed main dispatch SHA, never republishes an immutable version, and verifies npm, npx, and bunx anonymously."
actual_result: "Merged PRs #834 and #835; release run 30594784895 restored and verified v2026.7.30 from main in 9m41s; an independent token-free clean-cache verifier passed npm metadata, direct/package npx, bunx, and GitHub release checks on the first attempt."
fixed_version: 2026.7.30
